Request Time: 1 seconds
{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"50.201.197.218","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77311,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"03c9b0a311241718117001883ed0b966","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"Dina821\"] Yes, we had to pay $500 for the outside vendor fee for the photographer.&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1897852,"PostDate":1433341901,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"283278\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/283278-dina821\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">Dina821<\/span><\/a> Yes, we had to pay $500 for the outside vendor fee for the photographer.<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"rebeccalightsey@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"74.190.197.204","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1405539863,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-279045.jpg?_r=1434956018","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"facebook"},"FormattedName":"RebeLight","Id":279045,"Name":"RebeLight","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"66.65.74.207","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77311,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"594fdf511e740f59a4bc7f05493a0d90","RawContent":"[quote name=\"RebeLight\" post=\"1897753\" timestamp=\"1433269949\"]\n@[member=\"AshleyNYC323\"] &amp;amp; @[member=\"Dina821\"] Here&#039;s Pastor York&#039;s email address: rickandsuzanneyork@[member=\"gmail\"].com. \n\nAshley--I didn&#039;t try to get around the outside vendor fee...they just didn&#039;t charge it.  I would just ask your WC about it!\n\nDina--I&#039;m not sure if he can do a legal ceremony or not.  I believe you have to go through the Dominican government just like you do in the US.  He does have you both sign a document and two witnesses sign as well.  \n\nGood luck![\/quote]Thank you!","Attachments":[],"Id":1898017,"PostDate":1433598332,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>RebeLight, on 02 June 2015 - 02:32 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"282492\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/282492-ashleynyc323\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">AshleyNYC323<\/span><\/a> & @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"283278\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/283278-dina821\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">Dina821<\/span><\/a> Here's Pastor York's email address:\u00a0<a>rickandsuzanneyork@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"219734\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/219734-gmail\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">gmail<\/span><\/a>.com.\u00a0<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Ashley--I didn't try to get around the outside vendor fee...they just didn't charge it. \u00a0I would just ask your WC about it!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Dina--I'm not sure if he can do a legal ceremony or not. \u00a0I believe you have to go through the Dominican government just like you do in the US. \u00a0He does have you both sign a document and two witnesses sign as well. \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Good luck!<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>Thank you!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"ashley225@gmail.com","IpAddress":"66.87.117.140","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1426931385,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-282492.jpg?_r=1436650511","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"facebook"},"FormattedName":"AshleyNYC323","Id":282492,"Name":"AshleyNYC323","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"206.74.64.116","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77311,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":3,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"5d902862493b0206043d366a8c407b68","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Hi Ladies!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I recently got married at Now Larimar on May 21st with 35 guests.&amp;nbsp; I wanted to write a review on here since this site was soooo much help for me.&amp;nbsp; Yeomandry was my wedding coordinator, and she was very sweet.&amp;nbsp; She did everything how I asked, and was so patient!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I got my hair and make up down by Krystie Ann, who was absolutely amazing.&amp;nbsp; She was so professional, did incredible work, and I loved my hair and make up.&amp;nbsp; It stayed perfectly the whole night! Some of my bridesmaids got their hair and make up done at the spa which turned out absolutely stunning!&amp;nbsp; I did my hair and make up trial through the spa as Krystie Ann was not available, and I loved it.&amp;nbsp; The woman was sooooo sweet, and absolutely amazing at her job.&amp;nbsp; She did exactly what I showed her in the picture.&amp;nbsp; I think you are golden whether you use a private hair and make up artist or the spa.&amp;nbsp; We were all very happy.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We had our ceremony at the fountain at 4, which was very nice.&amp;nbsp; We had a symbolic ceremony by my husband&#039;s uncle. It felt very private.&amp;nbsp; I really liked the setting.&amp;nbsp; We had the guitarist who was great, and everything was very smooth and organized.&amp;nbsp; We brought an ipod with a few songs we wanted on it. The flowers also came out beautiful.&amp;nbsp; They did a great job on the bouquets and corsages.&amp;nbsp; We brought our own programs, but did not do any extra decorations. They placed the programs all nicely on the chairs for us.&amp;nbsp; I do not think you need a lot decorations there.   The setting is very pretty.&amp;nbsp; We did not do the wooden walkway, and I think it was still great. The only negative was that the fountain flooded (which was the ONLY time I saw it do that).&amp;nbsp; Luckily, it flooded after the ceremony.&amp;nbsp; It just limited our pictures a bit in front of the fountain.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;For cocktail hour we had spring rolls, chicken taquitos, sushi, and mozzarella canape.&amp;nbsp; Everyone loved the cocktail hour food&amp;nbsp; (especially the spring rolls).&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We had our reception at Castaways.&amp;nbsp; I absolutely loved Castaways, but was a disappointed as there was a wedding on the beach right by castaways. I only really noticed it during dinner however as we could hear their music.&amp;nbsp; There was a party on the beach that night which may have pushed our weddings closer together. But, when our music started we could not hear theirs any longer.&amp;nbsp; We brought shells down for the centerpieces, and rented tall vases.&amp;nbsp; We had them fill the vases half with shells, and then used their pink and orange stargazers as the flowers in the centerpieces.&amp;nbsp; We also brought a Mr &amp;amp; Mrs sign for the sweetheart table,&amp;nbsp; our own cake topper, table number holders\/brought starfish with the seating assignments on them, two large signs for decoration, table runners, luggage tag favors, champagne flutes, and a cake cutter.&amp;nbsp; Everything was set up perfectly.&amp;nbsp; The centerpieces were just how I asked them to be.&amp;nbsp; Dinner was good. The shrimp cocktail appetizer was excellent, the cream of mushroom soup was ok (I did not care for it, but most of my guests did), the sangria was excellent, steak\/lobster was good, and cheesecake was great.&amp;nbsp; However, people were getting up to dance right after the cheesecake was served.&amp;nbsp; The waiters removed the cheesecake before it was eaten while people were dancing.&amp;nbsp; The cake was delicious.&amp;nbsp; We had vanilla cake with chocolate filling.&amp;nbsp; However, again, the waiters removed the cake before a lot of people tasted it since they were dancing.&amp;nbsp; The waiters and bartenders were sooooo friendly though.&amp;nbsp; The service was excellent&amp;nbsp; (just a little too quick at times haha)!!&amp;nbsp; The waiters even got on the dance floor at the end of the night which was sooo fun!&amp;nbsp; All of our guests loved them.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We had the resort DJ, and I thought he was awesome.&amp;nbsp; We had given him a general list of songs, and he did a great job.&amp;nbsp; The MC was adorable.&amp;nbsp; She was a bit quieter than I thought she would be, but she was great at getting everyone up to dance. We also had the fire dancers.&amp;nbsp; They had chairs set up on the side of castaways for us to watch the fire dancers.&amp;nbsp; The dancers were incredible!&amp;nbsp; I was just slightly disappointed as random resort guests stopped to watch.&amp;nbsp; This was completely understandable, as they probably did not realize it was a private show.&amp;nbsp; However, they were seated in the seats that were set up for us.&amp;nbsp; Our wedding coordinator did not ask them to move.&amp;nbsp; We ended up sitting on the wood deck in front of the chairs that were set up.&amp;nbsp; Again, not a big deal, but something for future brides to be aware of.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We brought a friend down with us who does photography to do our pictures.&amp;nbsp; We did get the included wedding ceremony pictures which came out very nice, but it does cost extra to get the cd of pictures.&amp;nbsp; What is included in the package is just the printed out pictures.&amp;nbsp; We also used the resort videography, which came out nice. We got a 20% off deal which you guys should look for. We paid under $800 for a full day from getting ready all the way through the reception with a video trailer as well.&amp;nbsp; Julio was so great to work with.&amp;nbsp; He was sooo sweet and professional, he was just swamped with weddings. You can tell he truly cares about his job.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I have seen some brides ask about excursions on here. We did a few excursions.&amp;nbsp; We actually booked a private party boat for the day after our wedding which was absolutely amazing! It was our favorite thing! I booked it through Wilfrid from seapro.&amp;nbsp; He speaks great English.&amp;nbsp; We emailed back and forth a few months before the wedding.&amp;nbsp; I had met him when we did a site visit previously.&amp;nbsp; I would highly recommend him.&amp;nbsp; We booked two excursions with him. He was fabulous!&amp;nbsp; If you would like some information his email is Wilfridstamour2005@yahoo.fr.&amp;nbsp; If you do not want to book an excursion before, don&#039;t worry!&amp;nbsp; There are a ton of vendors booking excursions there.&amp;nbsp; I do not think you get a better price for booking early, we had just wanted to reserve a private party boat, so we figured we should book early.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I was also very nervous about my wedding dress on the airplane.&amp;nbsp; Everyone was very nice. The flight attendants waited until everyone was seated and then put it in one of the empty overhead bins. So don&#039;t stress!&amp;nbsp; Everyone wants to help a bride.&amp;nbsp; My dress was silk, and wrinkled easily.&amp;nbsp; It was incredibly wrinkled by the time we got to the resort!&amp;nbsp; The resort did an amazing job at steaming it.&amp;nbsp; So don&#039;t worry if it gets wrinkled on the trip.&amp;nbsp; They will fix it!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Finally, our travel agency was Wright Travel Agency. They did an amazing job.&amp;nbsp; Patty and Kristin responded to emails almost immediately, were soooo nice and patient, and all of our guests loved them as much as we did.&amp;nbsp; I could not have imagined planning this without them.&amp;nbsp; They were truly amazing, and two of the nicest people!&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I hope this helps!&amp;nbsp; Please feel free to ask me any questions.&amp;nbsp; Overall, there were a few minor things, but we had a wonderful wedding!!!!!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1898569,"PostDate":1434321113,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Hi Ladies!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I recently got married at Now Larimar on May 21st with 35 guests.\u00a0 I wanted to write a review on here since this site was soooo much help for me.\u00a0 Yeomandry was my wedding coordinator, and she was very sweet.\u00a0 She did everything how I asked, and was so patient!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I got my hair and make up down by Krystie Ann, who was absolutely amazing.\u00a0 She was so professional, did incredible work, and I loved my hair and make up.\u00a0 It stayed perfectly the whole night! Some of my bridesmaids got their hair and make up done at the spa which turned out absolutely stunning!\u00a0 I did my hair and make up trial through the spa as Krystie Ann was not available, and I loved it.\u00a0 The woman was sooooo sweet, and absolutely amazing at her job.\u00a0 She did exactly what I showed her in the picture.\u00a0 I think you are golden whether you use a private hair and make up artist or the spa.\u00a0 We were all very happy.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We had our ceremony at the fountain at 4, which was very nice.\u00a0 We had a symbolic ceremony by my husband's uncle. It felt very private.\u00a0 I really liked the setting.\u00a0 We had the guitarist who was great, and everything was very smooth and organized.\u00a0 We brought an ipod with a few songs we wanted on it. The flowers also came out beautiful.\u00a0 They did a great job on the bouquets and corsages.\u00a0 We brought our own programs, but did not do any extra decorations. They placed the programs all nicely on the chairs for us.\u00a0 I do not think you need a lot decorations there.\u00a0\u00a0 The setting is very pretty.\u00a0 We did not do the wooden walkway, and I think it was still great. The only negative was that the fountain flooded (which was the ONLY time I saw it do that).\u00a0 Luckily, it flooded after the ceremony.\u00a0 It just limited our pictures a bit in front of the fountain.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>For cocktail hour we had spring rolls, chicken taquitos, sushi, and mozzarella canape.\u00a0 Everyone loved the cocktail hour food\u00a0 (especially the spring rolls).<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We had our reception at Castaways.\u00a0 I absolutely loved Castaways, but was a disappointed as there was a wedding on the beach right by castaways. I only really noticed it during dinner however as we could hear their music.\u00a0 There was a party on the beach that night which may have pushed our weddings closer together. But, when our music started we could not hear theirs any longer.\u00a0 We brought shells down for the centerpieces, and rented tall vases.\u00a0 We had them fill the vases half with shells, and then used their pink and orange stargazers as the flowers in the centerpieces.\u00a0 We also brought a Mr & Mrs sign for the sweetheart table,\u00a0 our own cake topper, table number holders\/brought starfish with the seating assignments on them, two large signs for decoration, table runners, luggage tag favors, champagne flutes, and a cake cutter.\u00a0 Everything was set up perfectly.\u00a0 The centerpieces were just how I asked them to be.\u00a0 Dinner was good. The shrimp cocktail appetizer was excellent, the cream of mushroom soup was ok (I did not care for it, but most of my guests did), the sangria was excellent, steak\/lobster was good, and cheesecake was great.\u00a0 However, people were getting up to dance right after the cheesecake was served.\u00a0 The waiters removed the cheesecake before it was eaten while people were dancing.\u00a0 The cake was delicious.\u00a0 We had vanilla cake with chocolate filling.\u00a0 However, again, the waiters removed the cake before a lot of people tasted it since they were dancing.\u00a0 The waiters and bartenders were sooooo friendly though.\u00a0 The service was excellent\u00a0 (just a little too quick at times haha)!!\u00a0 The waiters even got on the dance floor at the end of the night which was sooo fun!\u00a0 All of our guests loved them.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We had the resort DJ, and I thought he was awesome.\u00a0 We had given him a general list of songs, and he did a great job.\u00a0 The MC was adorable.\u00a0 She was a bit quieter than I thought she would be, but she was great at getting everyone up to dance. We also had the fire dancers.\u00a0 They had chairs set up on the side of castaways for us to watch the fire dancers.\u00a0 The dancers were incredible!\u00a0 I was just slightly disappointed as random resort guests stopped to watch.\u00a0 This was completely understandable, as they probably did not realize it was a private show.\u00a0 However, they were seated in the seats that were set up for us.\u00a0 Our wedding coordinator did not ask them to move.\u00a0 We ended up sitting on the wood deck in front of the chairs that were set up.\u00a0 Again, not a big deal, but something for future brides to be aware of.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We brought a friend down with us who does photography to do our pictures.\u00a0 We did get the included wedding ceremony pictures which came out very nice, but it does cost extra to get the cd of pictures.\u00a0 What is included in the package is just the printed out pictures.\u00a0 We also used the resort videography, which came out nice. We got a 20% off deal which you guys should look for. We paid under $800 for a full day from getting ready all the way through the reception with a video trailer as well.\u00a0 Julio was so great to work with.\u00a0 He was sooo sweet and professional, he was just swamped with weddings. You can tell he truly cares about his job.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I have seen some brides ask about excursions on here. We did a few excursions.\u00a0 We actually booked a private party boat for the day after our wedding which was absolutely amazing! It was our favorite thing! I booked it through Wilfrid from seapro.\u00a0 He speaks great English.\u00a0 We emailed back and forth a few months before the wedding.\u00a0 I had met him when we did a site visit previously.\u00a0 I would highly recommend him.\u00a0 We booked two excursions with him. He was fabulous!\u00a0 If you would like some information his email is Wilfridstamour2005@yahoo.fr.\u00a0 If you do not want to book an excursion before, don't worry!\u00a0 There are a ton of vendors booking excursions there.\u00a0 I do not think you get a better price for booking early, we had just wanted to reserve a private party boat, so we figured we should book early.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I was also very nervous about my wedding dress on the airplane.\u00a0 Everyone was very nice. The flight attendants waited until everyone was seated and then put it in one of the empty overhead bins. So don't stress!\u00a0 Everyone wants to help a bride.\u00a0 My dress was silk, and wrinkled easily.\u00a0 It was incredibly wrinkled by the time we got to the resort!\u00a0 The resort did an amazing job at steaming it.\u00a0 So don't worry if it gets wrinkled on the trip.\u00a0 They will fix it!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Finally, our travel agency was Wright Travel Agency. They did an amazing job.\u00a0 Patty and Kristin responded to emails almost immediately, were soooo nice and patient, and all of our guests loved them as much as we did.\u00a0 I could not have imagined planning this without them.\u00a0 They were truly amazing, and two of the nicest people!\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I hope this helps!\u00a0 Please feel free to ask me any questions.\u00a0 Overall, there were a few minor things, but we had a wonderful wedding!!!!!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"cwright1320@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"72.230.115.231","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1388150678,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"Cwright","Id":275744,"Name":"Cwright","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"170.218.219.22","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77311,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"d7d4b85f5fb26c3432f2976c63f8fc67","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"WAVA8312\"] How are your plans coming along? We are right around the corner from our date.... I&#039;m getting excited :)&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1898672,"PostDate":1434460165,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"282440\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/282440-wava8312\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">WAVA8312<\/span><\/a> How are your plans coming along? We are right around the corner from our date.... I'm getting excited <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"feliciajones411@me.com","IpAddress":"170.218.219.21","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1418912679,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281438.jpg?_r=1418928163","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":150,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Dominican2015","Id":281438,"Name":"Dominican2015","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"54.212.162.231","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77311,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"cfb4f991e4aabf5e302d008fe32cdc2e","RawContent":"@[member=\"Cwright\"] did you just pay a set price for the boat or a per person price?  Do you think it would be too much to do the boat for an afternoon excursion the day before the wedding?  Also, did you have a dinner with your group the night before the wedding?","Attachments":[],"Id":1898734,"PostDate":1434523001,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"275744\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/275744-cwright\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">Cwright<\/span><\/a> did you just pay a set price for the boat or a per person price?  Do you think it would be too much to do the boat for an afternoon excursion the day before the wedding?  Also, did you have a dinner with your group the night before the wedding? \r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"swiens1@uco.edu","IpAddress":"157.142.25.168","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1421299345,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"sjw015","Id":281734,"Name":"sjw015","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"206.74.64.116","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77311,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"92399b51193f75bb9c2e2ac5f9c2b96c","RawContent":"@[member=\"sjw015\"] did you just pay a set price for the boat or a per person price?  Do you think it would be too much to do the boat for an afternoon excursion the day before the wedding?  Also, did you have a dinner with your group the night before the wedding?[\/quote]\n\n\nWe paid per person for the party boat. I think it would be too much to do the night before the wedding as there was a lotttt of alcohol involved. It was a big party. I know there are dinner cruises you could do but I am not sure how much those are? \n\n\nAlso we booked a dinner at capers the night before which was really nice and easy! We did this two days before. They let us book or for 34 people and we were at two large tables. Obviously not private but it worked out really great!!","Attachments":[],"Id":1898824,"PostDate":1434582470,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"281734\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/281734-sjw015\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">sjw015<\/span><\/a> did you just pay a set price for the boat or a per person price?  Do you think it would be too much to do the boat for an afternoon excursion the day before the wedding?  Also, did you have a dinner with your group the night before the wedding?[\/quote]<br><br>\nWe paid per person for the party boat. I think it would be too much to do the night before the wedding as there was a lotttt of alcohol involved. It was a big party. I know there are dinner cruises you could do but I am not sure how much those are? <br><br>\nAlso we booked a dinner at capers the night before which was really nice and easy! We did this two days before. They let us book or for 34 people and we were at two large tables. Obviously not private but it worked out really great!!\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"cwright1320@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"72.230.115.231","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1388150678,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"Cwright","Id":275744,"Name":"Cwright","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"50.8.84.124","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77311,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"eaf954ef55977a3df96ddb24be53ae37","RawContent":"Hi Brides! My fianc\u00e9 is really wanting a hot towel shave before the wedding. Has anyone that has gotten married at Now had their future husbands get this service done outside the resort? The spa does not offer a men&#039;s shave. Any help is appreciated! Thanks!","Attachments":[],"Id":1898945,"PostDate":1434820128,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Hi Brides! My fianc\u00e9 is really wanting a hot towel shave before the wedding. Has anyone that has gotten married at Now had their future husbands get this service done outside the resort? The spa does not offer a men's shave. Any help is appreciated! Thanks!\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"dibo930@aol.com","IpAddress":"50.8.84.124","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1432767962,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-283278.jpg?_r=1439577895","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"facebook"},"FormattedName":"Dina821","Id":283278,"Name":"Dina821","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"142.67.2.225","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77311,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"27503fe4325caa00786d17520f045a95","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Hey Ladies!! I sent off my deposit yesterday .. still haven&#039;t heard back from the WC but i know that is not unusual! haha While im waiting im starting to look at the costs of having a bar at the reception .. and im wondering .. i am contemplating going with the \"your moments\" package because i will get that complimentary, and then just do add-ons for the private reception, and extra people, because all the other stuff like getting your hair done, etc. doesn&#039;t appeal to me anyways since we are all just going to do each others hair that day..&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;my question is, im thinking of having a relaxed pool reception, so with that you have to do the buffet, so i am looking and it says for the international private bar it costs $12 per person, per hour!! Thats quite a expensive little bill. .&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;im trying to do this as cost effective as possible .. but looking at spending $3,000 for food and drinks .. when technically that stuff is already included in a your ticket price blows my mind .. does anyone have any suggestions for how they managed to have a cost effective wedding and still have a great time?? Im wondering if it would be more cost effective if we did this:&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Ceremony at the Fountain @ 4pm&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Private Dinner at the Carnival Buffet @ 6pm (they will reserve tables for you, just wont be a private dinner) (i think we will have more than 25 people so we have to go to the carnival if that&#039;s the case, otherwise you can reserve an a la carte restaurant if its available)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Relaxed pool reception from 7-10 with the music and dancing&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;has anyone else just done the non-private dinner and then only did the dancing reception??&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;any feedback is greatly appreciated :)&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1899193,"PostDate":1435140965,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Hey Ladies!! I sent off my deposit yesterday .. still haven't heard back from the WC but i know that is not unusual! haha While im waiting im starting to look at the costs of having a bar at the reception .. and im wondering .. i am contemplating going with the \"your moments\" package because i will get that complimentary, and then just do add-ons for the private reception, and extra people, because all the other stuff like getting your hair done, etc. doesn't appeal to me anyways since we are all just going to do each others hair that day..<\/p>\n<p>my question is, im thinking of having a relaxed pool reception, so with that you have to do the buffet, so i am looking and it says for the international private bar it costs $12 per person, per hour!! Thats quite a expensive little bill. .<\/p>\n<p>im trying to do this as cost effective as possible .. but looking at spending $3,000 for food and drinks .. when technically that stuff is already included in a your ticket price blows my mind .. does anyone have any suggestions for how they managed to have a cost effective wedding and still have a great time?? Im wondering if it would be more cost effective if we did this:<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Ceremony at the Fountain @ 4pm<\/p>\n<p>Private Dinner at the Carnival Buffet @ 6pm (they will reserve tables for you, just wont be a private dinner) (i think we will have more than 25 people so we have to go to the carnival if that's the case, otherwise you can reserve an a la carte restaurant if its available)<\/p>\n<p>Relaxed pool reception from 7-10 with the music and dancing<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>has anyone else just done the non-private dinner and then only did the dancing reception??<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>any feedback is greatly appreciated <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"ton_03@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"142.67.2.225","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1430216976,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-282892.jpg?_r=1434622094","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":150,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"FutureMrsVanthof","Id":282892,"Name":"FutureMrsVanthof","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"142.177.67.248","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77311,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"8d397a90f7a9172db98375500ce11150","RawContent":"[quote name=\"MyJourneytoMrs\" post=\"1887493\" timestamp=\"1424885322\"]\nHello All!!\n \nI am actually in the process of securing my April 2016 date at the Now Larimar. I was curious to know if anyone has considered taking advantage of the complimentary package, and paying for add ons to make it everything you want? I&#039;m thinking of doing that vs. purchasing a package, if its more cost containing.\n \nAlso, is there any place I can go to actually see each of the available locations for ceremonies and receptions??[\/quote]Hi! I am also just securing my date for March 2016, and am thinking of doing the same.. Have you decided what you are doing ??","Attachments":[],"Id":1899460,"PostDate":1435520306,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>MyJourneytoMrs, on 25 February 2015 - 01:28 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'><p>Hello All!!<br>\n\u00a0<br>\nI am actually in the process of securing my April 2016 date at the Now Larimar. I was curious to know if anyone has considered taking advantage of the complimentary package, and paying for add ons to make it everything you want? I'm thinking of doing that vs. purchasing a package, if its more cost containing.<br>\n\u00a0<br>\nAlso, is there any place I can go to actually see each of the available locations for ceremonies and receptions??<\/p><\/div><\/div>\n<br>\nHi! I am also just securing my date for March 2016, and am thinking of doing the same.. Have you decided what you are doing ??\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"ton_03@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"142.67.2.225","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1430216976,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-282892.jpg?_r=1434622094","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":150,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"FutureMrsVanthof","Id":282892,"Name":"FutureMrsVanthof","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"99.192.104.48","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":77311,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"d266ed5dc8327cddd384aa40abd3ba5c","RawContent":"Hi ladies!\n\nOk I&#039;m having a little panic attach here! We are going in March 2016 and I JUST realized how extremely far away and inconvenient the \"deluxe garden view\" rooms are from the actual resort\/beach .. I&#039;m actually mad right now. We used a travel agent and I had been to the resort when it was Eden h and loved it, but we stayed in the Bravaro Building &amp;amp; Punta Cana Buildings!! \n\nMy question is, when I asked my agent how I can get us in the other buildings (still waiting on the $ to upgrade) she says \"I can&#039;t guarantee anything it&#039;s up to the resort when you get there\" which makes me so mad and wonder why the heck I used her in the first place!!!! I&#039;m wondering if i contact the resort if there is anything they will do for me??? I&#039;m so upset about this and we have 35 people going so I feel like someone should be helping us out here considering we are already paying $1900 a person to go here!! If I would have known this I probably wouldn&#039;t have chosen this resort .. I&#039;m so bummed :(","Attachments":[],"Id":1900980,"PostDate":1437598603,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Hi ladies!<br>\nOk I'm having a little panic attach here! We are going in March 2016 and I JUST realized how extremely far away and inconvenient the \"deluxe garden view\" rooms are from the actual resort\/beach .. I'm actually mad right now. We used a travel agent and I had been to the resort when it was Eden h and loved it, but we stayed in the Bravaro Building & Punta Cana Buildings!! <br>\nMy question is, when I asked my agent how I can get us in the other buildings (still waiting on the $ to upgrade) she says \"I can't guarantee anything it's up to the resort when you get there\" which makes me so mad and wonder why the heck I used her in the first place!!!! I'm wondering if i contact the resort if there is anything they will do for me??? I'm so upset about this and we have 35 people going so I feel like someone should be helping us out here considering we are already paying $1900 a person to go here!! If I would have known this I probably wouldn't have chosen this resort .. I'm so bummed <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/sad.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':(' \/> \r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"ton_03@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"142.67.2.225","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1430216976,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-282892.jpg?_r=1434622094","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":150,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"FutureMrsVanthof","Id":282892,"Name":"FutureMrsVanthof","IsOnline":false}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":208,"TotalPages":21,"CurrentPage":190,"NextPage":200,"PreviousPage":180,"LastPage":200},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
